Abstract = {Barcelona is a city of science and committed to science. As a result of
   this commitment, the Barcelona Citizen Science Office was created in
   2012, a pioneering initiative, both in Spain and in Europe, with the aim
   of consolidating existing citizen science projects and creating a common
   learning space for new initiatives. With a ten-year history and within
   the framework of the development of the Barcelona Science Plan
   2020-2023, a new stage is beginning that reinforces the integration of
   the principles of open science in the practice of participatory research
   as an open process of knowledge generation and search for solutions to
   the social and environmental challenges of urban environments.},
